# A two-stage amplifier: two common-emitter stages, each like `amplifier`, the first driving the second
# through CC, so that a 2 mV signal comes out about a volt, the right way up.
#
# Each stage is biased the same way: its divider holds its base near 2 V, so about 1.3 mA flows and
# its collector sits near 7 V. Each stage's emitter resistance sets its gain, RE1 or RE3 and the
# transistor's own 20 Ω, with the rest bypassed by CE1 or CE2.
#
# The first stage's load is not only RC1: CC hands its signal to the second stage's base, whose divider
# and transistor draw on it too, so the first stage sees RC1 in parallel with the second's input, about
# 2.3 kΩ, and gains about 20. The second sees RC2 in parallel with RL, 2.8 kΩ, and gains about 23.
# Each turns its input upside down, so the two together give about 480 the right way up, 54 dB.
#
# The MID meter is the first stage's output: its swing beside IN's and OUT's in the scope's legend is
# each stage's gain. `b` shows the gain against frequency, falling away below 100 Hz where the coupling
# and bypass capacitors stop passing the signal. Turn the generator past about 10 mV and the second
# stage clips.

speed 2m
start settled

gen       G1    2 5   2 10   sine 1k 2m
wire            2 5   8 5
capacitor CIN   8 5   10 5   1u
wire            10 5  15 5

resistor  R1    11 0  11 5   47k
resistor  R2    11 5  11 10  10k

resistor  RC1   17 0  17 3   3.9k
npn       Q1    17 3  15 5   17 7   2N3904
resistor  RE1   17 7  17 8   100
resistor  RE2   17 8  17 10  1k
wire            17 8  21 8
capacitor CE1   21 8  21 10  100u

wire            17 3  21 3
capacitor CC    21 3  23 3   1u
wire            23 3  23 5
wire            23 5  29 5

resistor  R3    25 0  25 5   47k
resistor  R4    25 5  25 10  10k

resistor  RC2   31 0  31 3   3.9k
npn       Q2    31 3  29 5   31 7   2N3904
resistor  RE3   31 7  31 8   100
resistor  RE4   31 8  31 10  1k
wire            31 8  35 8
capacitor CE2   35 8  35 10  100u

wire            31 3  35 3
capacitor COUT  35 3  37 3   1u
wire            37 3  40 3
resistor  RL    40 3  40 10  10k

battery   B1    45 0  45 10  12V
wire            11 0  45 0
wire            2 10  45 10
ground          2 10

label     in    2 5
label     mid   23 5
label     out   40 3
meter     IN    2 5   2 10
meter     MID   23 5  23 10
meter     OUT   40 3  40 10
